course: dictionary
lesson: 1594
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The word check can mean to look at something, a paper that pays money, or a mark like a tick. To know which one is meant, read the words around it: this is its context. «Checking before you challenge saves you from being wrong in front of everyone.» Here check means to look carefully to find out if something is right.
explain: Ask yourself what the sentence is about. If it is about money, a bill or a bank, check probably means a paper that pays money. If it is about safety, or making sure something is right, check means to look at it carefully.
explain: Always test your meaning by putting it into the sentence in place of the word. If it still makes sense, you have probably chosen the right meaning.
fact: To check means to look at something to see if it is right, safe or ready.
fact: A check can also be a paper you sign that pays money from a bank. In British English this is spelled «cheque».
fact: In the USA, «check» can mean the bill in a restaurant.
fact: A check can be a tick mark, like ✓, which shows that something is right or done. A check can also be a pattern of squares.
fact: «check out» can mean borrow books or pay at a shop, «check in» means arrive at a hotel or airport, and «check on» means look after someone.
exercise: «If someone tells you a hurtful thing another person said, check with that person directly.» What does check mean here? | Hurt the person back | *Find out if it is true by asking | Run away from them | Shout at them across the playground
exercise: In a restaurant, Mum says, «Can we have the check, please?» What does she want? | A ticket for the cinema | *The bill to pay | A pattern of squares | A plan for the day
exercise: Miss Patel says, «Check your spelling before you hand in your work.» What does check mean? | Make it longer | Read it out loud to the class | *Look carefully to see if it is right | Throw it away and start again
test: Gran opened the bank's envelope and found a check for fifty pounds. What is a check here? | *A paper that pays money from a bank | A ticket to the zoo | A walk to see if the path is safe | A dark pattern of squares
test: Ben's cat is going to the vet for a health check. What does check mean here? | A bill for the vet | A quick run in the park | *A careful look to make sure the cat is well | A stripy pattern on its fur
exam: «Check both ways before you cross the road.» What does check mean? | Pay for the crossing | Shout loudly to the cars | Walk very fast across the road | *Look carefully to make sure it is safe
